From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry <45913169+brpjerry@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] linux: touch palm cancel, contact area, pen rotation and proximity out

Apollo's Linux touch screen and pen tablet features, which its own uinput
devices had before Sunshine moved input onto libvirtualhid, applied to
LizardByte/libvirtualhid dd8153df:

- A cancelled touch contact turns into a palm (ABS_MT_TOOL_TYPE
  MT_TOOL_PALM) before it lifts, so libinput reports a touch cancel
  instead of a completed tap; the slot is a finger again for the next
  contact.
- Touch contacts carry their area (ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR/MINOR, from
  TouchContact's axes in viewport pixels).
- PenToolState has a barrel rotation, sent as ABS_Z.
- A pen that leaves or is cancelled leaves proximity (BTN_TOOL_* released,
  tip lifted, held buttons released and pressed again when it returns).
  A tool change takes the old tool out in its own frame first.
- Test hooks that run a sequence of operations on a pipe-backed
  touchscreen or pen tablet.
